  "finalText": "I built the toggle micro-interaction in the Main composition (800×600, 60 fps, 2 s). It starts off and toggles at 0.4 s, and everything has settled by 0.95 s.\n\n- **Toggle track**: grey (#c7c7cc) to green (#34c759), crossfading from 0.4 s to 0.8 s.\n- **Toggle knob**: a group holding a shadow, the white disc and the checkmark. It slides from left to right over 0.4–0.85 s with a Back Out ease, so it overshoots slightly and settles.\n- **Squash and stretch**: the knob stretches to 118×88 mid-travel, then squashes to 97×103 on arrival, and returns to 100×100.\n- **Checkmark**: a green stroke drawn on from 0.62 s to 0.92 s.\n\nThe critique scored it 100/100 with no issues, and the contact sheet confirms the sequence. The track and checkmark timing are my choices, not from a spec. Want a bouncier overshoot or a faster knob slide?"
